# Rust build output. cockpit/target alone is 1.2 GB against ~10 MB of real
# source, and this directory had no .gitignore of its own until 2026-08-28 —
# a single `git add -A` would have carried all of it permanently.
target/

# Elixir (ampd)
_build/
deps/
*.beam
*.ez
erl_crash.dump

# Node
node_modules/

# A world's authority state. `scripts/make-super-source-tar.sh` already
# excludes these from a source audit for the reason that applies here too —
# a dets table is a world, not source — and until now nothing stopped a
# `git add -A` from committing somebody's Loci and worktrees into history.
*.dets

# Packaged revision bundles — regenerable release freight, not history.
and-super-rev-*.zip
*.tar.gz

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Sabotage battery evidence. Append-only on disk, not in history: a run log
# is a measurement of one execution, and the bundle summarises every one it
# finds. Committing them would make the tree grow by ~50 KB per battery.
.sabotage-runs/
